
SELECTOR test_large_production_roots_fit_default_caps
ok - spawn and teardown complete full analysis under the default caps with two workers

SELECTOR test_pinned_shellcheck_stops_at_the_memory_cap
ok - pinned ShellCheck lints under the default caps and a file past its memory cap fails by name

SELECTOR test_version_probe_memory_is_capped
ok - ShellCheck's version probe obeys the memory cap before file analysis

SELECTOR test_version_probe_time_is_capped
ok - ShellCheck's version probe obeys the time cap before file analysis

SELECTOR test_root_deadline_names_the_root_and_reaps_the_tree
ok - a root pinned at the wall deadline fails by name, reaps its tree, and leaves the sentinel alive

SELECTOR test_root_memory_cap_fails_by_name
ok - a root stopped at its memory cap fails by name, naming the cap

SELECTOR test_worker_trees_stop_on_signal
ok - jobs=1 and jobs=2 stop complete worker trees with and without telemetry

SELECTOR test_memory_failures_remain_failures_without_retry
ok - watchdog and heap memory failures retain their status without retrying in both worker modes

SELECTOR test_refuses_to_lint_without_its_watchdog
ok - fm-lint refuses to run ShellCheck without its watchdog and lints once it has one

SELECTOR test_seeded_module_boundary_parity
ok - seeded dispatcher, adapter, production-owner, and test-local diagnostics preserve parity
